where x is the thickness of the carbide layer, t is the reaction time, and k is the growth rate constant, e.g. the layer thickness increases with the square root of time. This relationship is a hallmark of diffusion-controlled processes and has been confirmed experimentally for Al–C systems [ 19 ,  29 ,  30 – 31 ]. The temperature dependence of the growth rate is described by Arrhenius-type relationship given in Eq. ( 2 ): 2 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
