where k 0  (10 − 4  – 10 − 6  m 2 /s) is a pre-exponential factor, Q (120–350 kJ/mol), depending on fiber type, composition, and interfacial conditions [ 19 ,  29 ,  30 – 31 ]) is the activation energy for diffusion, R (8.314 J mol − 1  K − 1 ) is the universal gas constant, and T is the absolute temperature. By combining both equations the thickness of the carbide layer can be estimated according to Eq. ( 3 ): 3 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
